add('agentic','SASKI Agentic — End-to-End Agent Governance','De-risk agentic applications with input scanning, deterministic action enforcement, output scanning, and signed decision evidence.',hero('SASKI Agentic / Agent governance','Let agents reason.<br> Govern what happens next.','Place deterministic controls around agent input, proposed actions, and output before the application proceeds.')+section('End-to-end governance','Four stages. One governed agent path.',agentic_architecture,'soft')+section('At the execution boundary','An instruction is not an authorization.', '<div class="split"><p class="lead">Add a safety layer without asking the model to govern itself.</p><div><p>SASKI Agentic scans input, evaluates proposed actions against explicit rules before they touch a connected system, and scans output before returning the result. Your model handles interpretation and planning; your governance policy defines the permitted path.</p><p>Start with a bounded workflow, explicit permissions, configured input and output checks, and an approval process for consequential changes.</p></div></div>')+section('Policy checks','Make the action boundaries explicit.',cards([('Who','Identity & authorization','Check whether the requesting actor is permitted to perform the action.',''),('What','Scope & parameters','Evaluate the target, operation, and requested parameters against the allowed scope.',''),('When','Prerequisites & approval','Require applicable conditions and human authorization before execution.','')]),'soft')+section('A governed workflow','From proposed action to recorded decision.',flow)+section('Designed for operational teams','Start where actions have consequences.','<div class="split"><div><h3>Connected environments</h3><p>Discuss agent workflows across AV, smart buildings, IT networks, surveillance, and access systems.</p></div><div><h3>Define the integration boundary</h3><p>Coverage depends on routing the relevant inputs, actions, and outputs through the governed path. Identify bypass routes, approval handling, and failure behavior during integration.</p></div></div>'),'Product')

